>2. Personal &amp\; Medical Information\:</b><br> Names\, phone numbers\, and child profile details (including photos) are used for identification and emergency contact purposes. To ensure safety during transit\, we collect optional medical information such as blood type\, allergies\, medications\, and medical conditions. This sensitive data is only visible to authorized drivers and administrators assigned to your route.<br><br> <b>3. Emergency SOS Alerts\:</b><br> When an SOS alert is triggered by a driver\, the system captures the bus's exact coordinates and immediately notifies relevant parents and administrators. This emergency data is prioritized to ensure rapid response and child safety.<br><br> <b>4. Security &amp\; Storage\:</b><br> We use Firebase Authentication for secure logins and Firestore for encrypted data storage. Child photos are stored securely via Cloudinary. Access to sensitive data is restricted to authorized personnel based on secure role-based permissions.<br><br> <b>5. Third-Party Services\:</b><br> BusWatch utilizes Google Play Services (Maps &amp\; Location) and OsmDroid to provide mapping features. These services handle location data according to their respective privacy policies.<br><br> <b>6. Contact Us\:</b><br> If you have questions about this policy\, or if you wish to exercise your rights regarding your data\, please contact our support team at\:<br> Email\: <a href=mailto\:buswatch2@gmail.com>buswatch2@gmail.com</a><br><br> <b>Last Updated\:</b> May 2\, 2026<br><br>"<![CDATA[
        <b>Privacy Policy for BusWatch</b><br><br>

        Welcome to BusWatch. We are committed to protecting your personal information and your right to privacy.<br><br>

        <b>1. Location Data\:</b><br>
        We collect the bus\\'s real-time location and your child\\'s boarding status to provide accurate tracking. Your home location is used to calculate estimated arrival times and stop proximity alerts. This data is essential for the core functionality of the safety tracking system.<br><br>

        <b>2. Personal &amp\; Medical Information\:</b><br>
        Names\, phone numbers\, and child profile details (including photos) are used for identification and emergency contact purposes. To ensure safety during transit\, we collect optional medical information such as blood type\, allergies\, medications\, and medical conditions. This sensitive data is only visible to authorized drivers and administrators assigned to your route.<br><br>

        <b>3. Emergency SOS Alerts\:</b><br>
        When an SOS alert is triggered by a driver\, the system captures the bus\\'s exact coordinates and immediately notifies relevant parents and administrators. This emergency data is prioritized to ensure rapid response and child safety.<br><br>

        <b>4. Security &amp\; Storage\:</b><br>
        We use Firebase Authentication for secure logins and Firestore for encrypted data storage. Child photos are stored securely via Cloudinary. Access to sensitive data is restricted to authorized personnel based on secure role-based permissions.<br><br>

        <b>5. Third-Party Services\:</b><br>
        BusWatch utilizes Google Play Services (Maps &amp\; Location) and OsmDroid to provide mapping features. These services handle location data according to their respective privacy policies.<br><br>

        <b>6. Contact Us\:</b><br>
        If you have questions about this policy\, or if you wish to exercise your rights regarding your data\, please contact our support team at\:<br>
        Email\: <a href=\"mailto\:buswatch2@gmail.com\">buswatch2@gmail.com</a><br><br>
        <b>Last Updated\:</b> May 2\, 2026<br><br>
